        "date": "2026-11-12T16:41:51Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): a turning section on a mill-turn needs a turning post\n\nMaintainer's decision on PR #1265 (2026-11-12, \"Refuse it\"): a section\nthat turns the work - a turning op or an on-centre drill, as\nlathe_voice::voice_of reads it - posts only through a post whose\ndialect is turning (work_voice WorkSpindle). On a lathe or a mill-turn\na milling post would write it for the tool spindle; it is now refused\nby name on every post path, nothing written. Milling and C-axis\nsections on a mill-turn still post through a milling post; the shipped\nMill-turn machine's default post is unchanged.\n\n- posting_serves::refusal takes the world and, when the kind is\n  served, refuses the work-spindle sections a non-turning post would\n  write (one derivation for lathe and mill-turn).\n- lathe_workholding_mill_post: the mill-turn facing pin is now a\n  refusal (stricter): refused by name at the chuck limit too.\n- post_serves_kind: a mill-turn facing op through Haas (own post) and\n  Fanuc (document post) is refused on post_mounts, post_per_op and\n  post_setup; a turning post serves it.\n- lathe_cross_drill: the generate-only tests stay on the plain lathe;\n  only the posting test uses a mill-turn (review blocker 3).\n- lathe_work_spindle: the on-centre drill on a mill-turn through the\n  Fanuc mill post is now refused by name (was: posts).\n- lathe_stroke: the built-in Mill-turn's turning job selects Fanuc\n  Lathe, as the built-in Lathe's does.\n- turning_contour_stock: indent (review note).\n\nRefs #1232\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
